// Illogical Impulse — baked zellij config (issue #23).
//
// UNOWNED seam: upstream's dots ship NO zellij config, so this file can never
// collide with an upstream rsync --delete tree and is never `--delete`d. Delete
// it (or `~/.config/zellij/` entirely) and zellij reverts to its own built-in
// defaults — the change is fully additive + reversible per the Iron Law.
//
// Colour: this config carries only a NEUTRAL, Material-You-leaning theme block.
// The distro does NOT ship a per-emulator recolour script — upstream's
// applycolor.sh `apply_anyterm()` already OSC-broadcasts the live Material You
// palette to every /dev/pts, and the zsh/fish shells `cat` sequences.txt on
// start, so zellij (running inside any emulator) inherits the terminal palette
// terminal-agnostically. The `ii` theme below is only the fallback face used
// before/absent that OSC broadcast; we deliberately keep it muted so it never
// fights the emulator's own colours.

// ── behaviour ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The dev layout below is the default when you just run `zellij`.
default_layout "ii"

// Copy a mouse selection straight to the system clipboard (issue #23 ask).
copy_on_select true

// Keep pane frames + mouse on — the polished, discoverable default.
pane_frames true
mouse_mode true

// A generous scrollback for build logs / test output.
scroll_buffer_size 20000

// Roomier default scrollback dump target and sane session behaviour.
default_mode "normal"
// Don't nag on exit; a dev spins sessions up and down constantly.
on_force_close "quit"
// Show the startup tips once; power users can flip this off in their own copy.
show_startup_tips true

// NOTE: we deliberately do NOT `clear-defaults=true` — zellij's default
// keybinds are excellent and clearing them would be a hostile, non-additive
// surprise. We keep every upstream-zellij default and layer nothing on top of
// them here, so muscle memory from a vanilla zellij carries over untouched.

// ── theme (neutral fallback face; live colour arrives via terminal OSC) ──────
theme "ii"
themes {
    // A muted, near-neutral Material-You-leaning face. Uses ANSI-ish tones that
    // sit quietly under whatever palette the emulator's OSC sequences push, so
    // switching emulators or recolouring the wallpaper "just works" without a
    // distro recolour script (upstream's apply_anyterm owns that path).
    ii {
        fg "#d7cfcb"
        bg "#1a1512"
        black "#221c19"
        red "#e0897a"
        green "#a6c48a"
        yellow "#d8bd82"
        blue "#93b1c9"
        magenta "#c4a2c9"
        cyan "#8fc7bd"
        white "#ece0dd"
        orange "#e0a879"
    }
}
